RAG Architecture Specification
Infrastructure Copilot v1.0

1. Business Perspective
For Infrastructure Copilot, RAG is not a “knowledge chatbot” feature. It is the investigation intelligence layer that allows the product to reduce MTTR by grounding answers in customer-specific operational data.
The Infra Copilot-PRD explicitly positions Infrastructure Copilot as a multi-tenant AI-powered Infrastructure Intelligence Platform designed to reduce MTTR using retrieval, incident correlation, historical pattern matching, change analysis, knowledge retrieval, and guided troubleshooting. [Infra Copilot-PRD | Outlook]
The business reason RAG exists in this product:
Plain Text1Engineers waste time searching incidents, changes, KBs, runbooks, alerts, and service context.2 3RAG brings the right operational context to the AI before the AI responds.Show more lines
The internal Retrieval-Augmented-Generation-(RAG)-in-the-Real-World states that RAG enhances LLMs by retrieving relevant information from external data sources before generating responses, allowing models to fetch relevant documents, use them as context, and generate more grounded responses. [Retrieval-...Real World | SharePoint]
Co-founder challenge: Do not build RAG as “upload PDF and ask question.” That is demo architecture. For Infrastructure Copilot, RAG must retrieve from incidents, changes, CMDB, alerts, runbooks, RCA history, SOPs, and service dependency data.

2. Technical Architecture
Recommended RAG Pattern
For v1, use:
Plain Text1Hybrid Retrieval + Metadata Filtering + Reranking + Citation EnforcementShow more lines
Not naive vector search only.
Why? A-Practical-Guide-to-RAG--Architectures,-Techniques,-and-Framework-Selection states that early naive RAG divides documents into chunks, converts them into embeddings, stores them in a vector database, and retrieves using similarity search, but it has limitations such as weak understanding of document relationships, poor handling of complex reasoning, degraded retrieval quality at scale, and difficulty with domain-specific terminology. [A Practica...Selection | SharePoint]
The same source recommends hybrid retrieval, query rewriting, metadata filtering, and context compression for enterprise knowledge assistant scenarios. [A Practica...Selection | SharePoint]

